  partName: Bolt (3)
  description: The Bolt (3) is another tiny, thin-flat fastener located at the top-center-front
    of the engine, also made of Material.004, and serves a similar purpose to the
    Bolt (2). By securing key engine parts, it helps maintain engine performance
    and prevent potential damage. An interesting aspect of the Bolt (3) is its potential
    for being interchangeable with the Bolt (2), depending on the specific engine
    design and manufacturer specifications.
